3. Touch layer
--------------
Adapted from "Bedrock-style touch controls for Eaglercraft 26.2" by terry65536:
https://github.com/terry65536/bedrock-touch-ui
License: MIT — Copyright (c) 2026 terry65536.

The MIT permission text in LICENSE applies to that code. Jamal Craft changes:
  - options seeding gained a compressed synchronous fallback and ?touch= modes;
  - the overlay layout now respects safe-area insets (notches, rounded corners);
  - native-mode / forced-mode query switches were added;
  - all control sprites were replaced with original artwork drawn by
    tools/make_touch_sprites.py. No Mojang/Bedrock textures are redistributed.

The layer is disabled automatically if the client's option store cannot be
written; the client's own touch HUD then continues to work. It can be turned
off with ?touch=native (and forced on with ?touch=bedrock).


